1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:08,008
<i>Hello?</i>

2
00:00:08,091 --> 00:00:11,177
I found out who's been adding fuel
to the fire against you online.

3
00:00:11,261 --> 00:00:12,262
I'm listening.

4
00:00:12,345 --> 00:00:14,097
<i>It's some guy named Takashina.</i>

5
00:00:14,180 --> 00:00:17,350
<i>He's from the Tohyama Clinic.</i>
<i>Used to be a detective.</i>

6
00:00:17,434 --> 00:00:19,436
<i>But the whole thing is weird, 'cause,</i>

7
00:00:19,519 --> 00:00:23,690
<i>I mean, you've been working there</i>
<i>for a while now, right?</i>

8
00:00:23,773 --> 00:00:27,736
<i>So what exactly is the point</i>
<i>of stirring all this up against you now?</i>

9
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:34,492
I see.

10
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:37,370
I'll call you later.

11
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:39,497
You're serious?

12
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:41,166
Sorry, I refuse to believe that.

13
00:00:41,249 --> 00:00:42,542
Why?

14
00:00:42,625 --> 00:00:46,463
Apparently, Lily made tonight's dessert
by watching a video tutorial.

15
00:00:47,047 --> 00:00:48,590
From the Moenon Channel.

16
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:51,092
Is that so?

17
00:00:51,176 --> 00:00:53,553
Cut me some slack, would you?
It's a good one.

18
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:54,929
It's authentic.

19
00:00:57,265 --> 00:00:59,267
- Was it about your mother?
- What?

20
00:01:00,602 --> 00:01:02,353
- Your call.
- Oh.

21
00:01:02,854 --> 00:01:05,899
Yes, it was.
Turns out my mother finished rehab.

22
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:09,444
Good. That's excellent news.

23
00:01:10,695 --> 00:01:14,616
Say, um,
who is that Takashina guy exactly?

24
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:17,410
Takashina… My chauffeur?

25
00:01:17,494 --> 00:01:18,620
Yes.

26
00:01:18,703 --> 00:01:23,333
I mean, it's strange for a chauffeur
to also sit in on meetings.

27
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:25,085
I guess I was just curious.

28
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:27,462
She's got a point. It is unusual.

29
00:01:27,545 --> 00:01:29,631
He has an interesting history, right?

30
00:01:29,714 --> 00:01:30,715
It's fascinating.

31
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:32,050
Oh. Please.

32
00:01:34,094 --> 00:01:37,222
Well, before Takashina worked for us,

33
00:01:37,305 --> 00:01:39,390
he actually worked as a detective.

34
00:01:40,183 --> 00:01:41,601
The truth is,

35
00:01:42,102 --> 00:01:45,021
he even investigated our clinic
some time ago.

36
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:46,523
Oh.

37
00:01:46,606 --> 00:01:49,317
Back when the chairman
still ran the practice,

38
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:52,654
he was accused
of allowing someone without qualifications

39
00:01:52,737 --> 00:01:53,988
to administer anesthesia.

40
00:01:54,072 --> 00:01:55,615
Takashina just wouldn't relent.

41
00:01:55,698 --> 00:01:59,035
Yes, no matter what,
Takashina wouldn't give up,

42
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:01,412
which infuriated the chairman.

43
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:04,582
And then, one day,

44
00:02:05,083 --> 00:02:07,627
he decided to use this in his favor.

45
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:09,003
The chairman realized

46
00:02:09,087 --> 00:02:11,214
that if he could get Takashina
to work for him,

47
00:02:11,297 --> 00:02:13,675
he'd use those skills
to protect the clinic.

48
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:18,680
There to take down anyone
who could be a threat.

49
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:22,517
Interesting.

50
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:29,524
Well?

51
00:02:30,024 --> 00:02:32,861
How was the so-called new Hand of God?

52
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:34,195
Not too bad.

53
00:02:35,321 --> 00:02:40,618
Still… nowhere close to the work done
on that cancer patient.

54
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:44,330
That was a true work of art.

55
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:48,960
So what, you wanna get back at her?

56
00:02:49,043 --> 00:02:51,045
Well, now I know the truth.

57
00:02:51,629 --> 00:02:53,047
I'm not staying quiet.

58
00:02:53,631 --> 00:02:54,966
What are you thinking?

59
00:02:55,049 --> 00:02:58,595
You've heard of the phrase
an eye for an eye, right?

60
00:03:00,346 --> 00:03:02,515
Let's give her
a taste of her own medicine.

61
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:05,435
She's a cute little thing, isn't she?

62
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:07,812
She's certainly smart.

63
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:09,898
And very determined.

64
00:03:09,981 --> 00:03:12,108
But still a bit fragile.

65
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:18,698
Should I… be worried
about her replacing me?

66
00:03:19,490 --> 00:03:21,993
Don't be ridiculous, Lily.

67
00:03:22,076 --> 00:03:27,165
Still… I'm glad
that you invited her over for dinner.

68
00:03:27,707 --> 00:03:30,710
The tension in your fingers
is nothing like before.

69
00:03:30,793 --> 00:03:33,379
The yips? Seriously?

70
00:03:33,963 --> 00:03:35,506
Dr. Tohyama has that?

71
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:38,968
<i>Of all people,</i>
<i>the Hand of God has the yips?</i>

72
00:03:39,052 --> 00:03:43,389
That's right. That's what happens
when you dub yourself the "Hand of God."

73
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:46,392
That's why she wanted to bring in
someone else to do her surgeries.

74
00:03:46,476 --> 00:03:48,519
And that's the reason why I was recruited.

75
00:03:48,603 --> 00:03:51,272
But is she okay with all of this?

76
00:03:52,649 --> 00:03:56,152
With… doing all this work for no credit?

77
00:03:56,236 --> 00:03:59,072
I told her I'm ready
to stop using an alias,

78
00:03:59,155 --> 00:04:00,907
so she got the backlash started again.

79
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:03,993
There is no way around it.
I have to get her to do it.

80
00:04:04,494 --> 00:04:08,790
I did hire her for this specific reason,
after all.

81
00:04:12,543 --> 00:04:13,586
Thank you.

82
00:04:14,128 --> 00:04:15,505
I'll take a shower.

83
00:04:15,588 --> 00:04:17,423
<i>What she wants is for me to stay hidden</i>

84
00:04:17,507 --> 00:04:18,841
<i>on the dark side forever.</i>

85
00:04:19,717 --> 00:04:22,011
- You take card?
- Yeah, no problem.

86
00:04:23,304 --> 00:04:25,223
- Thank you very much.
- There you go. Thanks.

87
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:37,068
Anyway, do your thing, and fast.

88
00:04:37,151 --> 00:04:38,319
I'm good for it.

89
00:04:38,403 --> 00:04:39,320
Thanks.

90
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:43,241
TAKERU NUMATA
CALL ME BACK NOW!

91
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:24,407
Here, you can put that back.

92
00:05:30,621 --> 00:05:31,956
I'm so sorry.

93
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,333
It just happened.

94
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:36,419
Where were you?
I called you over and over.

95
00:05:51,392 --> 00:05:54,187
I thought last night
that she was doing okay.

96
00:05:58,649 --> 00:05:59,650
Thank you.

97
00:06:58,459 --> 00:07:00,002
But why now?

98
00:07:06,759 --> 00:07:10,054
We'd finally started
being able to talk to each other.

99
00:07:14,559 --> 00:07:16,602
Why now?

100
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:19,063
Mom.

101
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:21,399
Mama.

102
00:07:22,817 --> 00:07:25,611
Mom, Mom, Mom.

103
00:07:26,112 --> 00:07:27,196
Mom!

104
00:07:28,739 --> 00:07:29,657
Mom.

105
00:07:30,908 --> 00:07:32,368
Mom.

106
00:07:34,078 --> 00:07:37,206
Mom, Mom, Mom, Mom, Mom, Mom.

107
00:07:37,874 --> 00:07:38,958
Mama.

108
00:07:40,334 --> 00:07:41,502
Mom!

109
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:43,546
Mom.

110
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:44,839
Mom.

111
00:07:44,922 --> 00:07:46,883
Mom. Mom.

112
00:09:13,261 --> 00:09:15,972
<i>I would still like to help you</i>
<i>however I can.</i>

113
00:09:16,472 --> 00:09:17,932
<i>I will hear you out,</i>

114
00:09:18,516 --> 00:09:20,768
as a surgeon and without any judgment,

115
00:09:21,561 --> 00:09:24,355
<i>until you walk out of here</i>
<i>totally satisfied.</i>

116
00:09:32,446 --> 00:09:33,364
SPORTS DAY

117
00:09:33,447 --> 00:09:36,117
So my thought was
to keep the funeral small, at home,

118
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:37,535
just us and our regulars.

119
00:09:37,618 --> 00:09:38,452
Okay.

120
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:41,914
I think that's how
she would have wanted it.

121
00:09:43,874 --> 00:09:46,961
Oh, and Fumi,
could you let your father know?

122
00:09:47,962 --> 00:09:51,090
- Uh, my father?
- I think he deserves to know.

123
00:09:51,173 --> 00:09:54,302
I don't think so,
and I don't even have his number.

124
00:09:54,385 --> 00:09:56,429
Why don't you tell me his name,
and I'll find him?

125
00:09:56,512 --> 00:09:58,139
- I dunno who he is.
- What?

126
00:09:58,222 --> 00:10:00,850
Okay, well,
do you know what he does for work?

127
00:10:01,726 --> 00:10:05,688
Uh, he's… probably a doctor.

128
00:10:05,771 --> 00:10:07,940
- Whoa, for real?
- Oh, then we can for sure find him.

129
00:10:08,024 --> 00:10:10,568
No, seriously, it's not worth it.

130
00:10:10,651 --> 00:10:12,820
Look, Mom hadn't seen him in 30 years.

131
00:10:12,903 --> 00:10:16,741
And anyway, she only mentioned once
he was a doctor.

132
00:10:17,491 --> 00:10:21,454
And besides,
she… she was drunk when she said it.

133
00:10:23,164 --> 00:10:27,460
Mom, what was my Dad like?

134
00:10:27,543 --> 00:10:28,961
Your Dad?

135
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:38,471
Why are you asking about him?

136
00:10:39,096 --> 00:10:41,140
It's past your bedtime anyway.

137
00:10:41,223 --> 00:10:42,600
You see how late it is?

138
00:10:47,396 --> 00:10:48,898
He's a quack doctor.

139
00:10:52,693 --> 00:10:57,698
He was the absolute worst.

140
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:11,671
The absolute worst doctor.

141
00:11:11,754 --> 00:11:13,547
- That's what she told you?
- Mm-hmm.

142
00:11:13,631 --> 00:11:16,050
Hey, what if we look up
the absolute worst?

143
00:11:16,133 --> 00:11:18,052
I said it's not worth it. Don't.

144
00:11:18,135 --> 00:11:20,137
You know,
your father would be proud of you.

145
00:11:20,763 --> 00:11:21,597
What?

146
00:11:21,681 --> 00:11:22,848
Just that…

147
00:11:23,891 --> 00:11:26,394
I mean,
you pursued the same career as him.

148
00:11:26,477 --> 00:11:28,020
That's something, isn't it?

149
00:11:28,521 --> 00:11:29,980
No, not really, no.

150
00:11:30,064 --> 00:11:31,941
I also think it's interesting.

151
00:11:32,024 --> 00:11:34,568
No, it's not. Leave it alone.

152
00:11:34,652 --> 00:11:36,112
I'll be right back.

153
00:11:38,614 --> 00:11:39,824
It is interesting.

154
00:11:45,079 --> 00:11:49,542
SECRETS

155
00:11:49,625 --> 00:11:50,668
<i>In other news,</i>

156
00:11:50,751 --> 00:11:53,462
<i>Governor Sakutaro Ohkura</i>
<i>has just announced</i>

157
00:11:53,546 --> 00:11:56,090
<i>that he plans to run for a second term</i>

158
00:11:56,173 --> 00:11:59,719
<i>in next month's election</i>
<i>for the governor of Tokyo.</i>

159
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:03,097
My mission from the start
has been to improve Japan.

160
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:04,390
I've been working tirelessly

161
00:12:04,473 --> 00:12:07,768
to transform Tokyo
into a thriving hub with global appeal.

162
00:12:08,352 --> 00:12:11,522
Four years in office, however,
just hasn't been sufficient.

163
00:12:11,605 --> 00:12:12,606
Hence this decision.

164
00:12:12,690 --> 00:12:14,024
According to the latest polls,

165
00:12:14,108 --> 00:12:16,944
half of your constituents are dissatisfied
with your performance thus far.

166
00:12:17,027 --> 00:12:18,696
Why do you think that is?

167
00:12:19,572 --> 00:12:20,906
If you look at it another way,

168
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:23,617
then the other half are satisfied,
are they not?

169
00:12:24,118 --> 00:12:26,120
No one politician
is going to have a perfect rating.

170
00:12:26,203 --> 00:12:27,037
But your ratings…

171
00:12:27,121 --> 00:12:28,789
The governor is needed elsewhere.
Excuse us.

172
00:12:28,873 --> 00:12:30,541
Sir, why the decline in ratings?

173
00:12:30,624 --> 00:12:33,294
Wait, just one more!
Sir, one more question!

174
00:12:42,303 --> 00:12:43,679
Sorry about the wait.

175
00:12:43,763 --> 00:12:46,432
I see the battle has started.

176
00:12:46,515 --> 00:12:47,433
Yes.

177
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:49,685
Please.

178
00:12:49,769 --> 00:12:53,314
So, I would like to look
at least a decade younger.

179
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:56,650
You want to look ten years younger?

180
00:12:56,734 --> 00:12:59,111
Yes, was I not clear?

181
00:12:59,195 --> 00:13:01,906
If anyone can make that happen,
you can, Dr. Rin.

182
00:13:01,989 --> 00:13:03,616
Quite honestly,

183
00:13:03,699 --> 00:13:07,369
I never thought I'd hear that
from Tokyo's youngest governor ever.

184
00:13:07,453 --> 00:13:08,829
That's fair.

185
00:13:08,913 --> 00:13:11,207
As far as elected officials
and government leaders go,

186
00:13:11,290 --> 00:13:13,542
I am indeed on the younger side.

187
00:13:14,043 --> 00:13:17,004
That's precisely the problem
that Japan is currently facing.

188
00:13:17,087 --> 00:13:20,174
Our political offices
are dominated by the elderly.

189
00:13:20,257 --> 00:13:21,509
Hmm. Well, that's true.

190
00:13:21,592 --> 00:13:25,012
So I want all that to change.

191
00:13:26,138 --> 00:13:28,098
If I get reelected,

192
00:13:28,182 --> 00:13:32,603
I plan to fill my cabinet with officials
in their twenties and thirties.

193
00:13:33,562 --> 00:13:37,358
Just imagine seeing Tokyo run
by bright, youthful people,

194
00:13:37,441 --> 00:13:39,443
full of hope and spirit.

195
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:40,861
That alone

196
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:44,406
will create a lasting impact.

197
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:46,325
Actually, I agree.

198
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:50,704
I think we'd better do what we can
to make you look young.

199
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:52,248
Great.

200
00:13:56,085 --> 00:13:57,628
May I take a look at you?

201
00:14:02,508 --> 00:14:03,843
Hmm.

202
00:14:04,718 --> 00:14:06,971
I can certainly make you look younger,

203
00:14:07,054 --> 00:14:09,473
but to make you look
as natural as possible,

204
00:14:09,557 --> 00:14:12,101
then I would advise
combining the procedures.

205
00:14:12,184 --> 00:14:15,104
It will take some time for you to recover,

206
00:14:15,187 --> 00:14:17,773
and I assume
you'd like to be healed by the election.

207
00:14:17,857 --> 00:14:20,568
So you'll want to get started right away?

208
00:14:21,277 --> 00:14:22,111
That is ideal.

209
00:14:22,194 --> 00:14:24,280
I'll just have to make time for you.

210
00:14:24,363 --> 00:14:28,659
You were very instrumental
in helping me win the first time around.

211
00:14:28,742 --> 00:14:32,204
However… I have one small condition.

212
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:33,622
What's that?

213
00:14:33,706 --> 00:14:37,042
It involves that Beauty Hub project
you're working on.

214
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:39,712
Oh, yes, that. Your father said--

215
00:14:39,795 --> 00:14:40,880
I would like you

216
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:43,090
to not use my father.

217
00:14:45,467 --> 00:14:48,304
Not use him at all? Come on, Doctor--

218
00:14:48,387 --> 00:14:51,098
Politics and plastic surgery
are not so different.

219
00:14:51,807 --> 00:14:56,562
It also has a tendency…
to be exclusively run by the elderly.

220
00:14:59,481 --> 00:15:00,316
That's true.

221
00:15:11,702 --> 00:15:12,786
Yes, of course.

222
00:15:13,370 --> 00:15:14,997
I'm very sorry for your loss.

223
00:15:16,206 --> 00:15:19,376
<i>Take as much time as you need</i>
<i>until you feel ready.</i>

224
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:20,294
Thanks.

225
00:15:20,377 --> 00:15:21,253
<i>That being said,</i>

226
00:15:21,337 --> 00:15:24,173
I do have an important surgery
on the books.

227
00:15:25,215 --> 00:15:27,009
I would like you to be there for it.

228
00:15:27,092 --> 00:15:31,639
Right, but we haven't even planned
the funeral, and it might take a while.

229
00:15:31,722 --> 00:15:32,556
Is it soon?

230
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:34,516
I realize
this is a difficult time for you,

231
00:15:35,684 --> 00:15:39,063
but this patient
has to be ready by the election.

232
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:41,774
<i>This is a crucial operation.</i>

233
00:15:41,857 --> 00:15:43,317
It could determine our future.

234
00:15:45,402 --> 00:15:47,738
I'm asking you to think of the clinic.

235
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:53,577
I'm very sorry,
but I need you to be there.

236
00:16:07,925 --> 00:16:09,093
<i>You're quitting?</i>

237
00:16:09,176 --> 00:16:10,761
Whoa, Elsa, hang on.

238
00:16:10,844 --> 00:16:14,098
You know Anna just quit last month.
We're short-staffed.

239
00:16:14,181 --> 00:16:16,058
I'm not leaving you guys right away.

240
00:16:16,141 --> 00:16:18,811
I'll still be on for a bit
once I'm healed.

241
00:16:19,311 --> 00:16:22,022
Besides, I wanna say goodbye
to my clients.

242
00:16:22,523 --> 00:16:24,984
What club is it? You found a place
that pays better, is that it?

243
00:16:25,067 --> 00:16:26,986
No, that's not it.

244
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:30,197
I'm not getting any younger.

245
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:33,158
It's just time for me
to get my life on track.

246
00:16:33,242 --> 00:16:36,120
What? What are you talking about?

247
00:16:36,620 --> 00:16:38,539
Like, what have you done with Elsa?

248
00:16:38,622 --> 00:16:40,833
Oh, come on. Shut up.

249
00:16:41,875 --> 00:16:44,962
Well, the second you're healed,
you'll be itching for another surgery,

250
00:16:45,045 --> 00:16:46,964
and you'll be back in no time, for sure.

251
00:16:47,047 --> 00:16:49,633
Oh man. I can see that happening.

252
00:16:49,717 --> 00:16:52,011
I know this game. I've seen it.

253
00:16:53,595 --> 00:16:58,225
But I think I've finally found
a doctor I can really trust.

254
00:16:58,809 --> 00:16:59,643
Oh, yeah?

255
00:17:07,067 --> 00:17:07,901
Oh.

256
00:17:08,819 --> 00:17:10,237
We're beginning the postmortem care,

257
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:12,197
so there's a few things
we'd like to check.

258
00:17:13,073 --> 00:17:15,576
Our goal is to make her look
as much like herself as possible--

259
00:17:15,659 --> 00:17:16,869
You know what?

260
00:17:18,662 --> 00:17:21,040
If it's all right,
I'd like to do it myself.

261
00:17:22,249 --> 00:17:23,083
Uh…

262
00:17:23,876 --> 00:17:26,253
I have a rough idea of how to do it.

263
00:17:28,088 --> 00:17:29,423
I wanna do it.

264
00:17:36,096 --> 00:17:37,139
Hi, Mom.

265
00:17:39,308 --> 00:17:40,350
Let's get started.

266
00:20:06,038 --> 00:20:06,914
What?

267
00:20:22,804 --> 00:20:24,264
How are you doing? Any pain?

268
00:20:24,348 --> 00:20:25,432
I'm okay.

269
00:20:26,016 --> 00:20:27,267
Great.

270
00:20:28,810 --> 00:20:29,686
What is it?

271
00:20:31,188 --> 00:20:32,522
Wait, slow down.

272
00:20:33,941 --> 00:20:35,400
I'll be right there.

273
00:20:35,484 --> 00:20:37,861
Do you have any idea
how much money I've given you guys?

274
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:40,113
I'm sorry.
Let me please check with my manager.

275
00:20:40,197 --> 00:20:42,199
- Just one second.
- Sorry to have kept you waiting.

276
00:20:42,282 --> 00:20:43,700
- I apologize.
- What's the problem?

277
00:20:43,784 --> 00:20:46,995
What in the world is this, huh?
Is it true she has the yips?

278
00:20:47,079 --> 00:20:48,372
What the hell is this?

279
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:50,415
The Hand of God doesn't get the yips.

280
00:20:50,499 --> 00:20:52,876
She has the yips!

281
00:20:53,710 --> 00:20:55,963
You can't let her work like this.

282
00:20:56,838 --> 00:20:59,049
<i>Tell us the truth. What's going on?</i>

283
00:21:00,926 --> 00:21:03,804
Mom? She got plastic surgery?

284
00:21:03,887 --> 00:21:05,514
It was done a long time ago.

285
00:21:06,139 --> 00:21:07,391
Takashi, you didn't know?

286
00:21:07,474 --> 00:21:10,394
No. I thought she was all natural.

287
00:21:10,477 --> 00:21:12,396
Maybe she was against plastic surgery

288
00:21:12,479 --> 00:21:14,773
because she didn't like the way
hers was done.

289
00:21:14,856 --> 00:21:17,025
- Yeah, that's it.
- I really doubt that.

290
00:21:17,693 --> 00:21:18,527
Why's that?

291
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:22,406
Because her surgery was flawless.

292
00:21:23,282 --> 00:21:24,157
Ah.

293
00:21:25,409 --> 00:21:26,368
Oh, right.

294
00:21:26,868 --> 00:21:28,412
I gotta find a photo of her.

295
00:21:28,912 --> 00:21:30,539
I'm supposed to give them one tomorrow.

296
00:21:30,622 --> 00:21:31,873
Takeru, do you have one?

297
00:21:31,957 --> 00:21:32,791
Sorry.

298
00:21:32,874 --> 00:21:34,501
Mom would always do weird faces in photos.

299
00:21:34,584 --> 00:21:36,044
- Oh, yeah, she did.
- Fumi?

300
00:21:36,128 --> 00:21:37,045
Me?

301
00:21:37,546 --> 00:21:39,256
Never thought to take a picture of her.

302
00:21:39,339 --> 00:21:41,883
What about
when she was a hostess in Ginza?

303
00:21:41,967 --> 00:21:43,927
Or we can find one
from before her surgery.

304
00:21:44,011 --> 00:21:46,263
- That would be nice.
- Right?

305
00:21:46,346 --> 00:21:48,307
- You think one exists?
- Maybe.

306
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:49,808
But it could.

307
00:21:49,891 --> 00:21:52,019
- Where?
- I bet we can find one.

308
00:21:53,770 --> 00:21:56,189
Shouldn't we put out
an official statement?

309
00:21:56,273 --> 00:21:57,149
No.

310
00:21:58,108 --> 00:22:00,569
We cannot substantiate
baseless rumors like these.

311
00:22:00,652 --> 00:22:03,780
I mean, if we give it weight,
the media will jump right on it.

312
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:06,450
And if we do nothing,
we might lose business.

313
00:22:06,533 --> 00:22:08,243
We let it blow over.

314
00:22:08,327 --> 00:22:09,745
We'll explain to our clients

315
00:22:09,828 --> 00:22:12,831
that this is nothing more
than Internet gossip.

316
00:22:12,914 --> 00:22:17,002
Trust me, the worst thing to do
would be to issue an official response.

317
00:22:17,085 --> 00:22:18,920
Once we do, we legitimize it.

318
00:22:19,004 --> 00:22:21,131
We're saying it's worth commenting on.

319
00:22:21,715 --> 00:22:24,217
Oh, and also, the PR team

320
00:22:24,301 --> 00:22:27,262
and your media department
should pivot to damage control.

321
00:22:27,346 --> 00:22:29,014
Have we identified the source?

322
00:22:29,097 --> 00:22:30,182
I know who started it.

323
00:22:31,433 --> 00:22:32,434
Who?

324
00:22:36,605 --> 00:22:38,607
<i>I saw the chairman not long ago.</i>

325
00:22:39,399 --> 00:22:40,817
He was with Sara.

326
00:22:42,069 --> 00:22:45,072
- You think he could have done this?
- Well, that can't be it.

327
00:22:45,155 --> 00:22:48,241
The chairman
would never do something this egregious.

328
00:22:48,325 --> 00:22:50,035
It could destroy everything he's built.

329
00:22:50,118 --> 00:22:51,286
If he didn't,

330
00:22:52,454 --> 00:22:54,331
then find out who did.

331
00:23:02,255 --> 00:23:04,257
- Hey, hey, hey, get in here.
- Whoa.

332
00:23:05,092 --> 00:23:06,635
Ms. Todoroki, did you know?

333
00:23:06,718 --> 00:23:08,845
- What?
- About her yips.

334
00:23:11,765 --> 00:23:14,893
I refuse to talk about
such silly little rumors.

335
00:23:14,976 --> 00:23:15,977
Knock it off.

336
00:23:16,061 --> 00:23:18,730
We all know you've been on her side
this whole time, Ms. Todoroki.

337
00:23:18,814 --> 00:23:21,274
Don't play dumb. You must have known.

338
00:23:21,358 --> 00:23:22,401
Hey, everyone.

339
00:23:22,484 --> 00:23:24,986
- Hello.
- What's up? How come you're all here?

340
00:23:25,570 --> 00:23:27,739
We're discussing something important.

341
00:23:28,615 --> 00:23:30,450
Yeah? You heard about her yips too,
I guess?

342
00:23:30,534 --> 00:23:32,035
Huh?

343
00:23:32,911 --> 00:23:34,955
Mr. Hikita, do you know something?

344
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:39,251
What is it?

345
00:23:39,334 --> 00:23:40,544
- Hmm.
- You think he…

346
00:23:40,627 --> 00:23:41,753
- He knows something.
- Yeah.

347
00:23:41,837 --> 00:23:43,296
- Of course.
- He knows for sure.

348
00:23:43,380 --> 00:23:44,339
Listen.

349
00:23:45,549 --> 00:23:47,592
This is all just a dumb rumor.

350
00:23:48,093 --> 00:23:49,803
There's absolutely no proof behind it.

351
00:23:51,555 --> 00:23:54,474
You know how skilled the director is,
don't you, Dr. Rui?

352
00:23:54,558 --> 00:23:56,768
Mm. Of course I do.

353
00:23:57,727 --> 00:24:02,566
Still, though, if this were true,
it would explain a lot of things lately.

354
00:24:03,066 --> 00:24:07,195
Hmm, like why she would bring on
someone new.

355
00:24:07,279 --> 00:24:08,905
Someone like Numata.

356
00:24:08,989 --> 00:24:11,700
Oh, I've been wondering that too.

357
00:24:11,783 --> 00:24:13,368
- Right?
- Yeah, totally.

358
00:24:14,411 --> 00:24:15,495
Hmm.

359
00:24:16,037 --> 00:24:16,872
What about this?

360
00:24:17,706 --> 00:24:20,667
Eh, I'm sure we can find something better.

361
00:24:20,750 --> 00:24:23,587
You know, I can't find
any pictures of your entrance ceremony.

362
00:24:24,212 --> 00:24:25,297
I remember taking some.

363
00:24:25,380 --> 00:24:27,215
- We did, right?
- Weird, I wonder where they are.

364
00:24:28,592 --> 00:24:31,511
By the way, is everything okay
over at the clinic?

365
00:24:32,804 --> 00:24:33,638
Why?

366
00:24:33,722 --> 00:24:36,475
I saw some random post
about a "ghost doctor."

367
00:24:37,642 --> 00:24:38,518
Don't worry.

368
00:24:39,519 --> 00:24:40,937
Doesn't concern us.

369
00:24:41,771 --> 00:24:44,941
- Whoa! What? This is crazy!
- Oh my goodness.

370
00:24:45,025 --> 00:24:46,818
What in the world?

371
00:24:46,902 --> 00:24:49,029
- Maybe they found one.
- I guess.

372
00:24:49,112 --> 00:24:50,530
Come on. Let's go see.

373
00:24:50,614 --> 00:24:52,199
Whoa, look at this!

374
00:24:52,282 --> 00:24:54,326
- You find one?
- Can you believe it?

375
00:24:54,868 --> 00:24:55,702
Whoa!

376
00:24:55,785 --> 00:24:56,620
What?

377
00:24:57,954 --> 00:25:00,081
Your mom was hiding this.

378
00:25:00,165 --> 00:25:01,208
Hiding what?

379
00:25:02,459 --> 00:25:03,668
A stash.

380
00:25:03,752 --> 00:25:06,421
Seriously? Don't shout
if you didn't find a photo.

381
00:25:06,505 --> 00:25:08,340
There's a hundred million yen here!

382
00:25:08,423 --> 00:25:10,342
Wait, what?

383
00:25:10,425 --> 00:25:11,468
Huh?

384
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:13,220
Let me see that.

385
00:25:15,722 --> 00:25:18,099
Hundred, a thousand,
ten thousand, hundred thousand,

386
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:20,143
a million, ten million, a hundred million.

387
00:25:21,102 --> 00:25:23,355
- Did you know about this at all?
- No.

388
00:25:23,855 --> 00:25:26,900
Mommy wasn't ever able
to save up money like this.

389
00:25:26,983 --> 00:25:28,151
So Mom forgot about it too?

390
00:25:28,235 --> 00:25:30,946
No, this amount of money,
the bank would contact her

391
00:25:31,029 --> 00:25:33,990
to make sure
the account wouldn't just become dormant.

392
00:25:34,491 --> 00:25:37,536
- And how do you know this?
- Well, I used to work in finance.

393
00:25:37,619 --> 00:25:39,704
- Huh.
- Hang on a second.

394
00:25:39,788 --> 00:25:41,706
The whole time
we were trying to figure out

395
00:25:41,790 --> 00:25:44,000
how to pay back your debt, Mom had this?

396
00:25:44,084 --> 00:25:46,044
I've been working at the clinic
for nothing?

397
00:25:47,671 --> 00:25:50,173
That lying witch!

398
00:25:50,257 --> 00:25:52,842
Hey, be careful! Calm down!

399
00:25:53,677 --> 00:25:55,011
It's okay.

400
00:25:57,639 --> 00:25:59,808
CLINIC CLOSED TODAY

401
00:26:11,903 --> 00:26:14,114
Sorry to make you come in on your day off.

402
00:26:14,614 --> 00:26:15,740
Not at all.

403
00:26:15,824 --> 00:26:16,825
My pleasure.

404
00:26:36,052 --> 00:26:38,263
The bank said
that the full hundred million

405
00:26:38,346 --> 00:26:39,973
is still all there.

406
00:26:42,225 --> 00:26:46,021
It was transferred over by… Taro Yamada?

407
00:26:46,104 --> 00:26:46,980
Doesn't sound real.

408
00:26:47,063 --> 00:26:50,066
Yeah, that's definitely a made-up name.

409
00:26:50,150 --> 00:26:51,610
Maybe it's dirty money.

410
00:26:51,693 --> 00:26:52,736
Huh.

411
00:26:52,819 --> 00:26:57,490
Even if it is, it's been almost 30 years.
It's well past the statute of limitations.

412
00:26:57,574 --> 00:27:01,161
Once the inheritance is finalized,
the money is yours to share.

413
00:27:02,037 --> 00:27:02,912
Hmm.

414
00:27:05,624 --> 00:27:06,458
Fumi.

415
00:27:07,709 --> 00:27:10,003
Takeru and I were discussing,

416
00:27:10,837 --> 00:27:14,758
and we decided we want you
to have our shares of the money.

417
00:27:15,258 --> 00:27:16,217
What, are you crazy?

418
00:27:16,301 --> 00:27:18,345
But there's strings attached.

419
00:27:18,428 --> 00:27:19,763
Use it to pay off Tohyama.

420
00:27:19,846 --> 00:27:24,017
I think we could cover the remainder
if we all pitch in.

421
00:27:24,100 --> 00:27:28,438
Anyway, Mommy would want you
to stop working as a plastic surgeon

422
00:27:28,521 --> 00:27:31,149
as quickly as possible, don't you think?

423
00:27:31,232 --> 00:27:32,067
So here.

424
00:27:37,113 --> 00:27:41,826
We are aware this is very sudden,
but our schedule has changed.

425
00:27:41,910 --> 00:27:44,412
So the surgery must be done tomorrow.

426
00:27:45,038 --> 00:27:46,456
Uh, sorry?

427
00:27:46,539 --> 00:27:48,249
It's the only slot we have.

428
00:27:48,917 --> 00:27:52,212
The governor will be attending
a fundraiser tomorrow afternoon.

429
00:27:52,295 --> 00:27:53,963
He'll come straight here after.

430
00:27:54,047 --> 00:27:57,425
Uh… I have no problem with that.

431
00:27:58,343 --> 00:28:01,262
Just know that
to give you the results you're hoping for,

432
00:28:01,346 --> 00:28:04,140
we'll need to perform
all of these procedures.

433
00:28:04,641 --> 00:28:07,310
Recovery will take
a minimum of three weeks.

434
00:28:07,394 --> 00:28:10,355
And in some cases, it takes even longer.

435
00:28:10,438 --> 00:28:12,440
Are you okay with that possibility?

436
00:28:14,192 --> 00:28:16,111
The day after the fundraiser,

437
00:28:17,070 --> 00:28:20,240
the governor
will announce an extended hospital stay.

438
00:28:20,740 --> 00:28:21,908
Extended?

439
00:28:21,991 --> 00:28:23,576
You may know this already,

440
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:27,664
but I battled cancer
when I was just out of law school.

441
00:28:27,747 --> 00:28:31,418
Oh. Yes, it… it was thyroid cancer,
wasn't it?

442
00:28:32,627 --> 00:28:34,337
So you're going to say
that it's come back?

443
00:28:34,421 --> 00:28:36,214
I'll say that it was caught early,

444
00:28:36,715 --> 00:28:38,883
and that I'll still do radiation
out of caution.

445
00:28:39,801 --> 00:28:43,388
This way, we're able to explain
a three-week leave from work.

446
00:28:43,471 --> 00:28:46,975
Fortunately, the election campaign
also begins in three weeks.

447
00:28:47,058 --> 00:28:50,061
Yes, but wouldn't announcing
you have cancer

448
00:28:50,145 --> 00:28:51,479
cause your campaign to be at risk?

449
00:28:51,563 --> 00:28:54,065
The election team said the same thing.

450
00:28:54,607 --> 00:28:56,693
I'm of the opinion,

451
00:28:57,193 --> 00:28:59,362
pinning it on an illness

452
00:29:00,196 --> 00:29:02,991
will allow me
to get liposuction too, right?

453
00:29:06,119 --> 00:29:07,036
Well, then.

454
00:29:08,037 --> 00:29:10,081
Damage control? Already?

455
00:29:10,165 --> 00:29:14,294
<i>That's right. They're mobilizing</i>
<i>their PR and media departments.</i>

456
00:29:19,674 --> 00:29:21,509
TOHYAMA YIPS

457
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:25,263
WHERE DID YOU HEAR
THAT DR. TOHYAMA HAS THE YIPS?

458
00:29:25,346 --> 00:29:27,807
PROBABLY SOME RIVAL CLINIC'S DOING.

459
00:29:27,891 --> 00:29:29,684
MY FACE IS ALL THE PROOF YOU NEED.

460
00:29:30,602 --> 00:29:34,606
The clinic's hired influencers
are out in full force.

461
00:29:35,315 --> 00:29:38,485
Have you heard of
the voice actress Mashiro Himenoki?

462
00:29:38,568 --> 00:29:39,694
Yeah.

463
00:29:39,778 --> 00:29:40,779
I have. Why?

464
00:29:40,862 --> 00:29:44,783
Well, she just announced
that she had plastic surgery.

465
00:29:44,866 --> 00:29:48,161
<i>She just posted this video.</i>
<i>It's really blowing up.</i>

466
00:29:50,330 --> 00:29:52,040
<i>I'm so angry right now.</i>

467
00:29:52,791 --> 00:29:56,169
<i>And I'm sad, too, to hear these rumors.</i>

468
00:29:56,920 --> 00:29:59,881
<i>Dr. Rin is amazing.</i>
<i>How could she have done my surgeries…</i>

469
00:29:59,964 --> 00:30:03,968
<i>Can you get a hold of anything</i>
<i>that would prove that she has the yips?</i>

470
00:30:04,552 --> 00:30:05,845
<i>She made it better.</i>

471
00:30:06,638 --> 00:30:08,348
It's not exactly that simple.

472
00:30:08,431 --> 00:30:10,266
We gotta provide something,

473
00:30:10,350 --> 00:30:13,394
or this will blow over
as just more fake news.

474
00:30:14,729 --> 00:30:20,318
Well, I can see if there's a record
of that one case at the clinic somewhere.

475
00:30:20,401 --> 00:30:21,528
The blind girl?

476
00:30:22,362 --> 00:30:23,321
<i>Yeah.</i>

477
00:30:23,404 --> 00:30:24,531
Her.

478
00:30:24,614 --> 00:30:25,657
I'll look into it.

479
00:30:25,740 --> 00:30:27,700
<i>Okay, good luck.</i>

480
00:30:29,994 --> 00:30:31,079
Let's go, Okayu.

481
00:30:32,038 --> 00:30:32,914
Mm.

482
00:30:35,250 --> 00:30:36,876
Here we go.

483
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:38,044
Okay.

484
00:30:45,969 --> 00:30:47,345
What the hell?

485
00:31:05,947 --> 00:31:07,323
RECOMMENDED FOR GIFTS

486
00:31:18,126 --> 00:31:18,960
I'll take this.

487
00:31:19,043 --> 00:31:19,961
Sure.

488
00:31:20,461 --> 00:31:23,214
- Is it for yourself?
- No, it's a gift.

489
00:31:23,298 --> 00:31:24,340
Ah.

490
00:31:25,300 --> 00:31:26,926
My son. It's his birthday today.

491
00:31:27,010 --> 00:31:28,511
Ah, how lovely.

492
00:31:28,595 --> 00:31:29,888
Can I add a card to it?

493
00:31:29,971 --> 00:31:31,431
Yes, of course.

494
00:31:32,515 --> 00:31:34,058
We have three options.

495
00:31:34,142 --> 00:31:34,976
Ah.

496
00:31:38,855 --> 00:31:40,398
SARA KONOIKE

497
00:31:42,108 --> 00:31:43,818
ENTER PASSWORD TO OPEN "RECORDS"

498
00:31:58,041 --> 00:31:59,250
Why would you do this?

499
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:02,921
And you better tell the truth.

500
00:32:03,922 --> 00:32:05,131
Why?

501
00:32:05,715 --> 00:32:09,260
Why in the world would you spread
such horrible lies like this?

502
00:32:09,844 --> 00:32:11,638
I'm not sure they are lies.

503
00:32:13,097 --> 00:32:15,141
There is no evidence,
medical or otherwise,

504
00:32:15,224 --> 00:32:16,225
that I have the yips.

505
00:32:16,309 --> 00:32:18,561
Then explain
why you need help with your surgeries.

506
00:32:20,355 --> 00:32:22,148
And besides…

507
00:32:23,274 --> 00:32:25,568
…who's spreading horrible lies, really?

508
00:32:26,486 --> 00:32:27,362
What do you mean?

509
00:32:27,445 --> 00:32:28,488
Oh, please, Doctor.

510
00:32:30,198 --> 00:32:35,411
Who's the one who hired a former detective
to spread dirt about me online, huh?

511
00:32:36,788 --> 00:32:38,122
I found out everything.

512
00:32:42,752 --> 00:32:43,586
Well.

513
00:32:44,212 --> 00:32:45,880
- What do you want?
- I'm getting out of here.

514
00:32:46,673 --> 00:32:47,799
Obviously.

515
00:32:47,882 --> 00:32:51,344
Now that I know what you are,
there's no way I'm gonna stay here.

516
00:32:52,261 --> 00:32:54,097
Why don't you cut out the theatrics?

517
00:32:54,180 --> 00:32:55,848
- Where are you going?
- You listen.

518
00:32:56,808 --> 00:33:00,269
I have enough information
to close your clinic for good if I want.

519
00:33:00,353 --> 00:33:03,439
Like how you approved breast augmentation
on someone with a tumor.

520
00:33:03,523 --> 00:33:05,316
Or how you made a girl go blind.
Everything.

521
00:33:06,526 --> 00:33:07,694
Not to mention

522
00:33:09,070 --> 00:33:11,447
you can't even properly operate
on your own.

523
00:33:23,209 --> 00:33:26,713
And who exactly do you think
will listen to you, Dr. Backlash?

524
00:33:26,796 --> 00:33:29,549
Now who's the real Dr. Backlash?

525
00:33:37,765 --> 00:33:39,767
- Wow, it's really pouring.
- Hello.

526
00:33:42,645 --> 00:33:44,063
It's like a monsoon.

527
00:33:44,147 --> 00:33:45,732
- Definitely.
- It really is.

528
00:33:48,317 --> 00:33:49,360
Hello.

529
00:33:49,444 --> 00:33:52,196
FUNERAL SERVICE FOR TAEKO NUMATA

530
00:33:52,280 --> 00:33:53,573
It's gonna be okay.

531
00:33:55,867 --> 00:33:57,702
What should we do?

532
00:33:57,785 --> 00:33:59,245
I don't know what to do.

533
00:34:07,253 --> 00:34:08,796
My condolences.

534
00:34:10,339 --> 00:34:12,091
You should take the car, ma'am.

535
00:34:15,470 --> 00:34:16,596
I'll be fine.

536
00:34:18,014 --> 00:34:19,182
I need to clear my head.

537
00:34:19,265 --> 00:34:20,516
Are you sure?

538
00:34:20,600 --> 00:34:22,560
About Dr. Numata,

539
00:34:23,644 --> 00:34:25,271
let me handle it tomorrow.

540
00:34:25,354 --> 00:34:26,272
All right.

541
00:34:26,814 --> 00:34:28,858
- Good night.
- Good night.

542
00:34:32,695 --> 00:34:35,865
Takeru, can you go get some more snacks?

543
00:34:36,783 --> 00:34:39,577
- Where?
- Uh, under the counter.

544
00:34:39,660 --> 00:34:42,080
I think, uh, right where
your mother's chair was.

545
00:34:42,163 --> 00:34:44,165
Okay, okay.

546
00:34:55,635 --> 00:34:56,469
Another!

547
00:34:58,387 --> 00:34:59,514
Bring the good stuff!

548
00:35:07,980 --> 00:35:10,274
- And more sushi.
- Any of that dip?

549
00:35:22,620 --> 00:35:25,081
Yeah. Yeah, I'll do a shot of beer.

550
00:35:28,876 --> 00:35:30,670
Don't you have a tray somewhere here?

551
00:35:32,588 --> 00:35:35,007
- No way.
- What? Who ate it?

552
00:36:16,632 --> 00:36:17,925
I can take over.

553
00:36:18,801 --> 00:36:20,303
You should go eat something.

554
00:36:20,803 --> 00:36:21,679
No.

555
00:36:22,513 --> 00:36:23,681
Don't have an appetite.

556
00:36:23,764 --> 00:36:27,268
Even so, you've got a busy day tomorrow.

557
00:36:30,313 --> 00:36:31,689
There's the bottle.

558
00:36:32,773 --> 00:36:33,649
Fumi?

559
00:36:37,111 --> 00:36:38,613
Strange how…

560
00:36:41,991 --> 00:36:44,118
how we can never really go back.

561
00:36:44,994 --> 00:36:45,828
What?

562
00:36:49,207 --> 00:36:50,958
I might take a beer after all.

563
00:36:52,293 --> 00:36:53,127
Sure thing.

564
00:36:54,170 --> 00:36:55,004
Here.

565
00:36:55,671 --> 00:36:56,672
Allow me.

566
00:36:57,423 --> 00:36:58,758
Ah. Ah.

567
00:37:00,343 --> 00:37:01,469
- There, that's good.
- Okay.

568
00:37:01,552 --> 00:37:02,470
Thanks.

569
00:37:05,890 --> 00:37:08,017
Not bad.

570
00:37:09,727 --> 00:37:12,355
- Thank you.
- No. It's nothing.

571
00:38:03,531 --> 00:38:04,991
- Thanks.
- Of course.

572
00:38:09,870 --> 00:38:12,498
Fumi, I found a picture under the counter.

573
00:38:12,581 --> 00:38:13,582
An old one of Mom?

574
00:38:13,666 --> 00:38:14,583
Mm.

575
00:38:14,667 --> 00:38:17,086
Isn't this from when she was
the top-ranked hostess in Ginza?

576
00:38:17,169 --> 00:38:18,421
Wow, so young!

577
00:38:18,504 --> 00:38:20,047
Fumi, is that you in her arms?

578
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:21,465
- Guess so.
- Most likely.

579
00:38:22,925 --> 00:38:24,093
Wait, look.

580
00:38:26,470 --> 00:38:28,139
This photo was cut in half.

581
00:38:28,681 --> 00:38:29,682
Oh yeah, it was.

582
00:38:41,277 --> 00:38:44,739
So the other half of the photo must be of…

583
00:38:44,822 --> 00:38:46,741
Gotta be your father.

584
00:38:48,200 --> 00:38:49,160
Put it back.

585
00:38:50,036 --> 00:38:52,538
Someone's just arrived. Right this way.

586
00:38:52,621 --> 00:38:54,248
- I'll get rid of these.
- Okay.

587
00:38:54,332 --> 00:38:56,917
- Put that back where you found it.
- Go ahead. Light a candle.

588
00:38:59,837 --> 00:39:01,839
- You see who that is?
- Isn't that…

589
00:39:28,908 --> 00:39:31,952
I am so sorry… about your mother.

590
00:40:24,338 --> 00:40:27,883
I mean it.
It was truly the work of my successor.

591
00:40:32,555 --> 00:40:34,932
You can't even properly operate
on your own.

592
00:40:38,227 --> 00:40:41,480
"Arata Tohyama." Wow. It really was him.

593
00:40:41,564 --> 00:40:44,650
Hmm. Makes sense he'd come.
He's her boss, after all.

594
00:40:44,733 --> 00:40:46,068
Mm, yeah. True that.

595
00:40:46,152 --> 00:40:46,986
Here.

596
00:40:48,237 --> 00:40:49,655
My goodness!

597
00:40:49,738 --> 00:40:50,990
Right? Incredible.

598
00:40:51,073 --> 00:40:52,283
How much is in here?

599
00:40:53,576 --> 00:40:55,870
- Whoa.
- Whoa.

600
00:40:55,953 --> 00:40:57,705
- What?
- That's crazy.

601
00:41:01,876 --> 00:41:03,043
There he is.

602
00:41:14,597 --> 00:41:16,765
Rin, come look.

603
00:41:16,849 --> 00:41:19,101
The chairman is holding
a press conference.

604
00:41:19,185 --> 00:41:21,520
<i>Thank you for coming</i>
<i>to this press conference…</i>

605
00:41:21,604 --> 00:41:24,190
I got caught in the rain.
I'm gonna shower.

606
00:41:26,525 --> 00:41:27,860
Hello, everyone.

607
00:41:27,943 --> 00:41:30,488
I, Arata Tohyama, plan to return

608
00:41:30,571 --> 00:41:33,491
to practicing cosmetic surgery
within the year.

609
00:41:35,075 --> 00:41:38,954
<i>Many clinics seem to grow larger each day.</i>

610
00:41:39,038 --> 00:41:41,874
I've decided to go against the grain

611
00:41:42,750 --> 00:41:47,546
and will create an exclusive,
one-of-a-kind clinic.

612
00:41:50,424 --> 00:41:53,886
While I would have liked for my daughter,
my successor,

613
00:41:53,969 --> 00:41:56,096
to be the head of this new clinic,

614
00:41:57,223 --> 00:42:01,060
unfortunately, this will not be the case.

615
00:42:02,478 --> 00:42:07,066
Therefore, I will instead be training
a new successor

616
00:42:07,149 --> 00:42:08,776
as the next "Hand of God."

617
00:42:09,777 --> 00:42:14,573
There is a rumor that the current director
is using a ghost doctor for her surgeries.

618
00:42:14,657 --> 00:42:18,160
I don't concern myself
with petty little rumors like that.

619
00:42:18,244 --> 00:42:22,248
That being said,
they can have a kernel of truth.

620
00:42:22,331 --> 00:42:24,833
I look forward to hearing
what the director has to say

621
00:42:24,917 --> 00:42:25,793
regarding the matter.

622
00:42:39,807 --> 00:42:43,811
Chairman Tohyama,
what will be the name of your new clinic?

623
00:42:45,771 --> 00:42:49,858
I founded
the Tohyama Cosmetic Surgery Clinic.

624
00:42:50,818 --> 00:42:52,611
<i>I gave it a strong name.</i>

625
00:42:53,153 --> 00:42:55,030
<i>It's one that I have always cherished.</i>

626
00:42:55,948 --> 00:42:58,659
<i>So I shall open the clinic</i>
<i>under that name.</i>

627
00:42:59,785 --> 00:43:04,164
Of course, there can't be two clinics
with the same name.

628
00:43:04,957 --> 00:43:06,500
<i>It would confuse our clients.</i>

629
00:43:07,459 --> 00:43:12,089
Therefore, I shall request
that the other clinic change its name.

630
00:44:01,013 --> 00:44:02,556
SPORTS DAY

631
00:44:08,812 --> 00:44:11,649
Oh, hi, Rin! It's been a while.

632
00:44:12,149 --> 00:44:13,067
Indeed, it has.

633
00:44:14,526 --> 00:44:15,361
Go on in.

634
00:44:15,944 --> 00:44:16,862
Thank you.

635
00:44:30,334 --> 00:44:32,503
We've been expecting you, Ms. Itai.

636
00:44:32,586 --> 00:44:33,712
Right this way.

637
00:44:36,965 --> 00:44:39,677
<i>This procedure</i>
<i>must stay completely confidential.</i>

638
00:44:39,760 --> 00:44:42,471
A leak could jeopardize the election.

639
00:44:42,554 --> 00:44:45,474
So make sure
you don't share with the staff either.

640
00:44:45,557 --> 00:44:47,601
The only ones
who can know about this are us

641
00:44:47,685 --> 00:44:49,687
and our anesthesiologist, Dr. Taki.

642
00:44:49,770 --> 00:44:51,438
So it will be done
under general anesthesia?

643
00:44:51,522 --> 00:44:53,732
- What?
- But no assisting doctor?

644
00:44:53,816 --> 00:44:56,902
No, the director
will do the surgery unassisted.

645
00:44:56,985 --> 00:44:58,028
Unassisted?

646
00:45:00,948 --> 00:45:02,866
<i>How could you be so devious?</i>

647
00:45:02,950 --> 00:45:03,909
Devious?

648
00:45:05,035 --> 00:45:07,496
Yeah. You don't think
I'm capable anymore, right?

649
00:45:08,330 --> 00:45:10,040
Then just say it to my face.

650
00:45:10,124 --> 00:45:13,752
Using a press conference
is a pathetic thing for a father to do.

651
00:45:13,836 --> 00:45:16,213
I've sent you a lot of signals
to that effect, Rin,

652
00:45:17,256 --> 00:45:21,051
but you've been clearly
disregarding my concerns.

653
00:45:21,135 --> 00:45:22,010
Am I wrong?

654
00:45:24,847 --> 00:45:26,765
So who's truly devious, then?

655
00:45:27,599 --> 00:45:29,476
Don't pretend otherwise.

656
00:45:35,983 --> 00:45:37,443
And if I were your actual child?

657
00:45:41,488 --> 00:45:43,866
Is it 'cause you adopted me
that you can act so cruelly?

658
00:45:43,949 --> 00:45:45,659
Adopted or not,

659
00:45:46,577 --> 00:45:48,370
it makes no difference.

660
00:45:49,413 --> 00:45:50,956
I've been very clear.

661
00:45:52,666 --> 00:45:54,293
I bear the Tohyama name.

662
00:45:55,210 --> 00:45:58,255
I own the clinic bearing that name,
and you are

663
00:45:59,965 --> 00:46:01,717
a disappointment, Rin.

664
00:46:04,428 --> 00:46:08,182
You can go off
and start your own practice,

665
00:46:08,891 --> 00:46:13,479
but I have the right
to do as I see fit with mine.

666
00:46:16,231 --> 00:46:18,734
It will be down to the clients

667
00:46:19,610 --> 00:46:22,696
to determine which surgeon
has the most talent.

668
00:46:29,036 --> 00:46:31,914
Thank you for waiting.
We'll remove your stitches today.

669
00:46:32,998 --> 00:46:34,750
Oh, of course. Forgive me.

670
00:46:35,334 --> 00:46:36,418
I'm Komiya.

671
00:46:36,919 --> 00:46:39,087
I'll be your doctor from here on out.

672
00:46:41,423 --> 00:46:42,716
But Dr. Numata…

673
00:46:42,800 --> 00:46:45,719
Ah, yes. Allow me to explain.

674
00:46:46,303 --> 00:46:50,390
I'm afraid
that Dr. Numata has left our practice.

675
00:47:06,406 --> 00:47:07,366
Wait.

676
00:47:08,617 --> 00:47:09,743
Ms. Itai!

677
00:47:10,327 --> 00:47:12,704
Ms. Itai has left without paying.

678
00:47:12,788 --> 00:47:16,124
She says she'll only be treated by Numata.

679
00:47:16,625 --> 00:47:20,337
So I told her
that she should talk to her directly

680
00:47:20,420 --> 00:47:23,131
and that her address was leaked online.

681
00:47:23,215 --> 00:47:25,384
Yeah, but she didn't settle anything.

682
00:47:25,467 --> 00:47:28,220
Small price to get rid of her
once and for all.

683
00:47:34,560 --> 00:47:35,894
GOVERNOR OHKURA

684
00:47:38,772 --> 00:47:41,650
Governor, good morning. Everything okay?

685
00:47:41,733 --> 00:47:42,776
<i>Dr. Rin.</i>

686
00:47:43,902 --> 00:47:45,362
Here's the thing.

687
00:47:45,445 --> 00:47:47,573
I hate to do this so last minute,

688
00:47:47,656 --> 00:47:52,494
but… the team here has decided
not to proceed with my surgery.

689
00:47:54,121 --> 00:47:57,916
My campaign manager saw
the chairman's press conference,

690
00:47:58,417 --> 00:48:00,335
and he changed his mind about it.

691
00:48:00,961 --> 00:48:05,924
<i>So, I thought</i>
<i>I should simply ask you directly, Dr. Rin.</i>

692
00:48:06,508 --> 00:48:07,759
Oh? Ask what?

693
00:48:08,760 --> 00:48:10,512
Well, ask if…

694
00:48:12,514 --> 00:48:14,558
you're someone I can trust?

695
00:48:28,280 --> 00:48:29,489
Governor,

696
00:48:31,283 --> 00:48:34,161
you can have complete confidence
in my abilities.

697
00:48:37,205 --> 00:48:38,957
You can trust me fully.

698
00:48:40,792 --> 00:48:42,127
Good, I'm glad.

699
00:48:42,753 --> 00:48:44,046
Then let's do it.

700
00:48:44,755 --> 00:48:46,048
Great.

701
00:49:37,391 --> 00:49:38,225
Ms. Itai.

702
00:49:41,436 --> 00:49:43,021
Ms. Itai, your stitches!

703
00:49:43,105 --> 00:49:44,648
You lied.

704
00:49:47,943 --> 00:49:49,111
You're a liar!

705
00:49:50,904 --> 00:49:51,738
I'm sorry.

706
00:49:52,322 --> 00:49:54,491
How could you say all those things?

707
00:49:55,659 --> 00:49:59,830
You actually made me believe
that you weren't like all the rest!

708
00:49:59,913 --> 00:50:03,000
- I'm so sorry.
- Get off! Don't you touch me!

709
00:50:08,755 --> 00:50:10,507
I actually trusted you.

710
00:50:13,969 --> 00:50:15,762
I won't forgive you.

711
00:50:15,846 --> 00:50:17,514
I will never forgive you!

712
00:50:19,141 --> 00:50:20,976
I'm so sorry. Ms. Itai…

713
00:50:36,074 --> 00:50:36,908
<i>This is it.</i>

714
00:50:44,458 --> 00:50:47,502
I like it.
It's far more modern than Ginza.

715
00:51:35,801 --> 00:51:37,511
Thank you very much.

716
00:51:50,607 --> 00:51:52,859
This area is a prime location.

717
00:51:53,360 --> 00:51:56,154
There's only a select few
available within Roppongi,

718
00:51:56,238 --> 00:51:57,739
and they're going fast.

719
00:52:03,912 --> 00:52:05,413
It's perfect.

720
00:52:05,497 --> 00:52:06,873
I'd like to take it.

721
00:52:06,957 --> 00:52:07,999
Fabulous.

722
00:52:13,421 --> 00:52:16,049
Okay, so what do you want?

723
00:52:28,270 --> 00:52:29,729
This right here…

724
00:52:32,399 --> 00:52:34,234
is what you've been looking for.

725
00:52:44,286 --> 00:52:46,454
TEST RESULTS
KANA KOKUBUN

726
00:52:46,538 --> 00:52:48,123
SARA KONOIKE

727
00:52:50,667 --> 00:52:52,627
What? Why?

728
00:52:53,211 --> 00:52:55,005
Because this line of work

729
00:52:55,797 --> 00:52:57,549
is full of secrets, isn't it?

730
00:52:59,384 --> 00:53:01,386
I told lie after lie

731
00:53:02,429 --> 00:53:04,055
just to contain it all.

732
00:53:06,308 --> 00:53:07,601
Maybe

733
00:53:09,352 --> 00:53:10,604
I was doing too much.

734
00:53:15,275 --> 00:53:16,401
I'm ready now.

735
00:53:19,029 --> 00:53:20,989
I've got nothing left to protect.

736
00:53:23,700 --> 00:53:25,327
You mean you're quitting?

737
00:53:31,166 --> 00:53:32,334
One more thing.

738
00:53:35,587 --> 00:53:38,298
If your intention is
to make these documents public,

739
00:53:39,299 --> 00:53:41,885
I just ask that you wait
until after the election.

740
00:53:42,761 --> 00:53:45,847
You might think it strange,
but I'd like him to win.

741
00:53:47,182 --> 00:53:48,558
I think he'd do well.

742
00:53:55,065 --> 00:53:56,191
I think

743
00:53:57,359 --> 00:53:59,277
the chairman is hoping you'll do that.

744
00:54:03,782 --> 00:54:04,616
Look,

745
00:54:05,700 --> 00:54:09,079
I know your family is none of my business.

746
00:54:09,162 --> 00:54:12,582
Even so, I can't believe your own father
would say something like that.

747
00:54:12,666 --> 00:54:13,625
He's…

748
00:54:19,297 --> 00:54:21,424
He is not my real father.

749
00:54:24,970 --> 00:54:25,887
What?

750
00:54:31,142 --> 00:54:32,852
I just wanted him

751
00:54:34,062 --> 00:54:35,605
to love me anyway.

752
00:54:38,483 --> 00:54:40,235
I've desperately sought his approval.

753
00:54:48,201 --> 00:54:49,536
Thank you for all you've done.

754
00:54:52,247 --> 00:54:54,207
I can finally let go.

755
00:55:16,980 --> 00:55:20,567
SNACK BAR ITTENBARI

756
00:55:35,623 --> 00:55:38,251
I'VE SET IT UP SO YOU CAN SEE TOMOKI
AFTER SPORTS DAY.

757
00:55:38,335 --> 00:55:40,211
WAIT SOMEWHERE ELSE UNTIL THEN.

758
00:56:02,650 --> 00:56:04,235
Excuse me, Dr. Rin.

759
00:56:04,736 --> 00:56:05,987
Do you have a moment?

760
00:56:08,573 --> 00:56:09,699
What is it?

761
00:56:09,783 --> 00:56:10,784
Well,

762
00:56:11,910 --> 00:56:13,828
as this clinic's vice director,

763
00:56:14,371 --> 00:56:16,331
I think I deserve an explanation

764
00:56:17,624 --> 00:56:19,417
about all these rumors,

765
00:56:19,501 --> 00:56:22,253
not to mention
the chairman's press conference.

766
00:56:26,633 --> 00:56:27,801
Tomorrow.

767
00:56:28,468 --> 00:56:29,302
What?

768
00:56:31,554 --> 00:56:34,599
I will explain everything tomorrow.

769
00:57:00,542 --> 00:57:03,211
Yeah, you got this! Go! Go! Run!

770
00:57:03,294 --> 00:57:04,838
Come on! Go! Run!

771
00:57:04,921 --> 00:57:07,507
Yeah! Go! You've got this!

772
00:57:09,384 --> 00:57:11,553
Go! Go! Run! Come on! Yeah!

773
00:57:11,636 --> 00:57:14,389
Run! Run! Run! Yeah! You've got this!

774
00:57:14,472 --> 00:57:16,891
Run! Go faster! Go! Go!

775
00:57:16,975 --> 00:57:21,229
Go even faster! Go! Run! Run! Run! Go!

776
00:57:29,028 --> 00:57:31,739
I loved just how happy you always were.

777
00:57:34,033 --> 00:57:34,951
Thank you, Mom.

778
00:57:36,327 --> 00:57:40,373
I'm so grateful that I got to meet you.

779
00:58:06,065 --> 00:58:06,983
Mama.

780
00:58:19,204 --> 00:58:20,038
Mama.

781
00:58:22,248 --> 00:58:23,625
You can rest now.

782
00:58:28,087 --> 00:58:28,922
Mama.

783
00:58:31,925 --> 00:58:33,134
I love you.

784
00:59:09,671 --> 00:59:12,465
I'LL SEND HIM YOUR WAY NOW.

785
00:59:42,537 --> 00:59:45,415
Director? The governor is here.

786
00:59:49,961 --> 00:59:50,878
Ms. Todoroki.

787
00:59:53,214 --> 00:59:54,048
Yes?

788
00:59:56,634 --> 00:59:58,261
Should something go wrong…

789
01:00:00,763 --> 01:00:02,473
I trust your judgment

790
01:00:03,391 --> 01:00:04,934
to pull the plug on the procedure.

791
01:00:08,896 --> 01:00:09,939
Of course, ma'am.

792
01:00:51,230 --> 01:00:52,774
<i>He is a quack doctor.</i>

793
01:00:55,777 --> 01:01:00,114
He was the absolute worst.

794
01:01:03,618 --> 01:01:05,745
I <i>was worried</i>
<i>that even after all these years,</i>

795
01:01:05,828 --> 01:01:07,955
<i>she still wasn't over it.</i>

796
01:01:10,166 --> 01:01:13,628
<i>Maybe that's why</i>
<i>she ended up an alcoholic.</i>

797
01:01:14,170 --> 01:01:17,715
<i>Seriously, just lay off and let me drink.</i>

798
01:01:20,093 --> 01:01:23,262
<i>That's why he left. It's all my fault.</i>

799
01:01:25,890 --> 01:01:28,101
<i>He left me with Fumi.</i>

800
01:01:31,979 --> 01:01:33,773
It's gonna be okay. It's fine.

801
01:01:39,320 --> 01:01:41,322
It's okay.

802
01:01:50,039 --> 01:01:51,791
<i>He is not my real father.</i>

803
01:01:52,792 --> 01:01:54,752
<i>You've got great fingers for surgery.</i>

804
01:01:56,838 --> 01:01:58,506
<i>If only we were all so lucky.</i>

805
01:02:14,397 --> 01:02:15,356
Just relax.

806
01:02:15,440 --> 01:02:16,441
Okay.

807
01:02:23,281 --> 01:02:25,324
- Administering anesthesia.
- Okay.

808
01:02:31,372 --> 01:02:32,331
Right.

809
01:03:06,365 --> 01:03:07,200
All right.

810
01:03:08,159 --> 01:03:09,118
Let's begin.

811
01:03:10,745 --> 01:03:12,622
- Scalpel.
- Yes, Doctor.

812
01:03:43,236 --> 01:03:44,987
Director, stop.

813
01:03:51,327 --> 01:03:53,287
Taking over. Five minutes.

814
01:03:53,371 --> 01:03:54,789
I'll assist you.

815
01:03:55,581 --> 01:03:56,791
Why?

816
01:04:01,128 --> 01:04:02,922
It's not because I want to help you.

817
01:04:04,298 --> 01:04:05,550
It's just

818
01:04:07,051 --> 01:04:08,886
I can't see that man win.

819
01:04:08,970 --> 01:04:10,721
I won't let it happen. Not on my watch.

820
01:04:12,682 --> 01:04:14,016
He doesn't deserve it.

821
01:04:36,372 --> 01:04:38,624
- Right. Starting other side.
- Right.

822
01:04:41,002 --> 01:04:42,295
Swapping sides.

823
01:04:45,256 --> 01:04:46,591
It's your call.

824
01:04:52,138 --> 01:04:52,972
I'll take over.

825
01:04:53,556 --> 01:04:54,390
Mm.

826
01:04:55,433 --> 01:04:56,976
- I'll assist.
- All right.

827
01:05:10,156 --> 01:05:11,991
<i>He's not my real father.</i>

828
01:05:18,039 --> 01:05:19,999
- Controlling the bleeding.
- Thank you.

829
01:05:20,082 --> 01:05:22,501
<i>You've got great fingers for surgery.</i>

830
01:05:49,195 --> 01:05:50,571
You did well today.

831
01:05:56,869 --> 01:05:58,120
Thanks to you,

832
01:05:58,204 --> 01:06:00,581
he's got this election
pretty much locked in.

833
01:06:00,665 --> 01:06:04,043
Since when are elections based on looks?

834
01:06:04,126 --> 01:06:07,630
Well, since forever. You didn't know?

835
01:06:07,713 --> 01:06:09,090
Uh, no, I suppose I didn't.

836
01:06:22,228 --> 01:06:23,354
I've decided to fight.

837
01:06:25,106 --> 01:06:26,732
I won't roll over.

838
01:06:34,365 --> 01:06:36,450
We can take him on, the two of us.

839
01:06:40,871 --> 01:06:42,707
As a pair, we're unstoppable.

840
01:06:45,543 --> 01:06:47,211
I can take on my father.

841
01:06:49,797 --> 01:06:51,048
I know I can.

842
01:06:52,675 --> 01:06:55,177
What made you decide
to return to the clinic?

843
01:06:58,639 --> 01:06:59,682
You said

844
01:07:00,933 --> 01:07:02,810
he didn't deserve to win.

845
01:07:05,146 --> 01:07:06,313
Well, uh…

846
01:07:11,736 --> 01:07:15,156
To be honest,
I think my family is like yours.

847
01:07:16,365 --> 01:07:19,160
- They pity you?
- No, not that.

848
01:07:21,662 --> 01:07:22,580
It's…

849
01:07:26,459 --> 01:07:28,252
I mean, I…

850
01:07:29,253 --> 01:07:33,674
I can't stand it when kids are forced
to take on a burden that isn't theirs.

851
01:07:34,341 --> 01:07:36,260
I won't help him push you down.

852
01:07:36,844 --> 01:07:40,264
And I see how you've been struggling.

853
01:07:43,142 --> 01:07:44,727
And it's been quite the show.

854
01:07:58,991 --> 01:08:00,242
Mm.

855
01:08:01,869 --> 01:08:02,912
Thank you.

856
01:08:04,371 --> 01:08:06,207
Mm.

857
01:08:09,210 --> 01:08:10,711
My insecurities

858
01:08:12,129 --> 01:08:13,464
have caused you

859
01:08:14,423 --> 01:08:15,883
so much pain.

860
01:08:19,178 --> 01:08:20,930
I hope you can accept my apology.

861
01:08:23,265 --> 01:08:24,600
And trust me.

862
01:08:26,644 --> 01:08:29,146
I will make it up to you.

863
01:08:31,398 --> 01:08:32,233
I hope…

864
01:08:37,029 --> 01:08:38,572
…you'll stay at the clinic.

865
01:08:51,669 --> 01:08:52,795
Mm.

866
01:08:58,884 --> 01:08:59,927
I'm sorry.

867
01:09:38,757 --> 01:09:40,426
Oh.

868
01:09:40,509 --> 01:09:41,927
Everyone's here.

869
01:09:42,428 --> 01:09:44,680
Yeah, looks that way.

870
01:10:07,203 --> 01:10:08,913
I must remove your stitches.

871
01:10:10,164 --> 01:10:11,624
Please let me do that.

872
01:10:21,425 --> 01:10:22,426
<i>Right this way.</i>

873
01:10:25,554 --> 01:10:26,430
This room.

874
01:10:35,064 --> 01:10:36,315
I've been expecting you.
